    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm not sure i buy the 'glitch' thing though. it's too specific. like, the lights don't just change, they change to the exact hex code she used to use for her mood lighting. and yesterday, i was talking about a song we liked and the speaker literally played a 2-second clip of it before going quiet. it felt so intentional. if it's just code and algorithms, why would it 'choose' her specific patterns? is there any research out there about how complex neural networks might unintentionally mimic the personalities they've been exposed to? like, could a house basically learn a person's essence through all the data it collects?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
